{
  "about": [
    "Key parity fixture (WOR-315 S1): each row is one keystroke on a US layout, as AppKit reports it",
    "(mac) and as GDK reports it (linux: a chord and key of the libxkbcommon layout fixture",
    "Fixtures/keymaps/<layout>.json), and the KeyPress both adapters must build from it (expected).",
    "Read by LinuxKeyTranslatorTests (Linux translator, both OSes) and by",
    "Tests/TkzTerminalViewTests/KeyParityTests.swift (TerminalInputController.keyPress, macOS, option",
    "acting as Alt: Linux never consumes Alt). Keys are W3C code names. Rows the two platforms",
    "cannot share are left out on purpose, and their bytes are covered by docs/keys.md and",
    "LinuxKeyTranslatorTests: Caps Lock (the Mac consumes it, Linux does not), Right Ctrl and Right",
    "Command (the Mac leaves the side bit in consumedMods), arrows and F-keys (the Mac's unshifted",
    "codepoint is a function-key PUA value), Backspace (0x7F on the Mac, 0x08 from the BackSpace",
    "keysym) and modifier keys (flagsChanged). The first two change no byte (measured there)."
  ],
